From: nomorecoolnicknames <nomorecoolnicknames@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 18:57:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] NetworkPolicyManagerService: ignore carrier config
 changes for an invalid subId

A dual-SIM phone with one slot empty broadcasts
ACTION_CARRIER_CONFIG_CHANGED with an invalid subId. There is no
subscriberId to find, but the Slog.wtf turns it into an error dialog on
every boot of a userdebug build. Log it at debug level instead. The
other wtf sites iterate active subscriptions, whose subIds are valid.
---
 .../com/android/server/net/NetworkPolicyManagerService.java | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/net/NetworkPolicyManagerService.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/net/NetworkPolicyManagerService.java
index 02a3b6f39..16f11fbae 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/net/NetworkPolicyManagerService.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/net/NetworkPolicyManagerService.java
@@ -1602,8 +1602,12 @@ public class NetworkPolicyManagerService extends INetworkPolicyManager.Stub {
                     if (subscriberId != null) {
                         ensureActiveMobilePolicyAL(subId, subscriberId);
                         maybeUpdateMobilePolicyCycleAL(subId, subscriberId);
-                    } else {
+                    } else if (SubscriptionManager.isValidSubscriptionId(subId)) {
                         Slog.wtf(TAG, "Missing subscriberId for subId " + subId);
+                    } else {
+                        // A dual-SIM device with an empty slot broadcasts the change
+                        // with an invalid subId; there is no subscriberId to find.
+                        Slog.d(TAG, "Ignoring carrier config change for invalid subId " + subId);
                     }
 
                     // update network and notification rules, as the data cycle changed and it's
